{{!
    @template tool_vae/course_link_page

    The page "Rattacher une fiche au cours", between its header or heading and the footer: a notification (the sub-system
    of competencies is off, or no record is imported), or what the page is for and the table of the records.

    Every text comes from the context, already worded by tool_vae\output\course_link_page. The template holds no logic: the
    states exclude one another before. Every text is escaped (double braces), except two keys of HTML (triple braces):
    noticehtml, a notification made by the core ($output->notification()); tablehtml, a table drawn by the template
    tool_vae/table (the codes, dates and counts in it are escaped by the template tool_vae/cell_content; the buttons are made
    by the core).

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * none

    Context variables required for this template:
    * noticehtml - false, or HTML: the notification of the state (off, no record)
    * intro - false, or a string: what the page is for
    * tablehtml - false, or HTML: the table of the records

    Example context (json):
    {
        "noticehtml": false,
        "intro": "Attach a record to this course: its competencies are added to the course.",
        "tablehtml": "<table class=\"generaltable\"><tbody><tr><td>DEMOBLOCS (RNCP)</td></tr></tbody></table>"
    }
}}
{{#noticehtml}}
{{{noticehtml}}}
{{/noticehtml}}
{{#intro}}
<p>{{intro}}</p>
{{/intro}}
{{#tablehtml}}
{{{tablehtml}}}
{{/tablehtml}}
